sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg–Turing wavelength for Fractofusus misrai at 63 µm (565 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 87.6/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 of the 63 µm (6.33e-05 m, log10 = -4.199) detail-scale model for Fractofusus misrai at Mistaken Point, 565 Ma (chronoseries 1/1). The linear dispersion fit is unchanged (Pearson r = 0.999999999, RMSE = 0.00375). The saturated Fourier wavelength now lengthens with D_u: 69.8 µm, 82.2 µm, 94.0 µm at D_u = 0.08, 0.12, 0.18, above the analytical curve and in the same direction. The nominal saturated peak remains 73.7 µm against the linear 63.3 µm. The render's interior is an oblique chevron of vanes on the siltstone spindle rather than the Pass 1 spot lattice. GIF versus the CC BY photograph scores 84.6 on the orientation / radial-FFT / coherency comparison. Specimen spindle aspect 1.70 versus render 1.12; gradient-angle KS D = 0.121. Equal diffusion and the 2×2 subcritical domain still decay. Fifty-one detail wavelengths fit in the 3.275 mm organ module and fifty-two do not. Overall 87.6/100 (faithfulness 87.4, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 731414 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 1693932873ca663e510a863079db4f8619b75720cf94ad9ff2f14d49d198de79 (sha256 1693932873ca663e510a863079db4f8619b75720cf94ad9ff2f14d49d198de79), spec_fingerprint b7aed75670ec58eb2e24b6b33d4964b84814f0e27b8d16305477ab4160932f43. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b7aed75670ec58eb2e24b6b33d4964b84814f0e27b8d16305477ab4160932f43; artifact_sha256: 1693932873ca663e510a863079db4f8619b75720cf94ad9ff2f14d49d198de79; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=749222e73e20900f..., datasets/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0/fractofusus_misrai_specimen.jpg=e423fba39900f0b8..., datasets/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=6b331d726b68779e..., datasets/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=365f45ca2b96a3cb..., datasets/fractofusus_misrai_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=00bdda7655784bfa...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-fractofusus-misrai-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: instability at a finite critical wavenumber selects a stationary wavelength. | Gehling & Narbonne 2007 name Fractofusus misrai from Mistaken Point, mid-Ediacaran ca. 575–560 Ma. | Hoyal Cuthill & Conway Morris 2014: fractal, self-similar rangeomorph branching consistent with osmotrophy. | Mitchell et al. 2015: multigenerational stolon-like reproduction plus waterborne propagules.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg a=0.09, b=0.85, D_u=0.12, D_v=2.40, grid spacing set so analytical λ_c = 6.33e-05 m. Not the slot 1251 parameters. | Pass 2 display weights oblique vanes by the activator envelope. The vane angle is a display choice; the wavelength it carries is the model's. | Three saturated fields measure how the Fourier peak moves with D_u.; transfer_boundary: Evaluated at 63 µm on one Mistaken Point photograph. Not transferred to Fractofusus andersoni, to the 3.275 mm module's kinetics, or to Cambrian segments.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured 63 µm pigment ocellus. The length is the evaluation scale. | Does not claim the saturated peak equals 63.3 µm. It is longer, and the shift is plotted. | Does not claim a second assessor. R3 is open.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Still one assessor. A second provider has not scored Pass 2.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'The nonlinear wavelength (73.7 µm at nominal D_u, 82.2 µm on the sweep grid) is not brought back to 63.3 µm by a weakly nonlinear correction. The shift is reported rather than removed.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Specimen comparison is one unscaled bedding-plane photograph. Branch spacing on the fossil is not in micrometres.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.876"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; R3 still open)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

